{"qid":"Q10791211","names":["Kingdom of Mrauk U"],"title":"Kingdom of Mrauk U","endonym":null,"capsule":"The Kingdom of Mrauk U was founded in 1430 by Narameikhla (Min Saw Mon) on the coastal plain of Arakan (modern Rakhine State, Myanmar), after he recovered his throne from the Ava kingdom with Bengali Sultanate military assistance, temporarily making Mrauk U a vassal of Bengal. From the mid-fifteenth century it became fully independent and developed into a major Bay of Bengal maritime power, controlling the coast from the Sundarbans to the Gulf of Martaban at its apogee around 1599–1603, and hosting Arab, Portuguese, Dutch, and Danish traders; European visitors compared the capital's wealth to Venice. Chittagong fell to the Mughal Empire in 1666, curtailing Arakan's eastern trade dominance. The Konbaung dynasty of Burma conquered Mrauk U on 2 January 1785, ending the kingdom and beginning the persecution of the Rohingya Muslim population.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Core territorial control over coastal Arakan is attested in Burmese and Bengali chronicles and Portuguese records; the northern extent of control over Chittagong and the eastern limit toward the Irrawaddy delta are more approximate and varied considerably across the kingdom's history.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Kingdom of Mrauk U","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Mrauk_U"},{"label":"Britannica: Mrauk-U","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/Mrauk-U"}],"britannica":"place/Arakanese-Kingdom-of-Mrohaung","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Kingdom of Mrauk U","rulers":[{"qid":"Q6862585","name":"Min Saw Mon","